  "id": "Compound::DB00622 - Gene::801",
  "verbalization": "Nardipine, a dihydropyridine, is linked to Calm1 through a shared pathway involving calcium channel blockers. The evidence suggests that Nicardipine, as part of the dihydropyridine class, binds to Calm1 via a common intermediate, Felodipine. This connection is reinforced by the presence of a lowest common ancestor between Nicardipine and Felodipine, which is the Methyl Ester category. The relationship between Nicardipine and Calm1 is thus mediated through the dihydropyridine class and Felodipine, which are both part of the broader calcium channel blocker family. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism where dihydropyridine drugs, through their interaction with calcium channels, may influence the activity of Calm1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
